course: dictionary
lesson: 4879
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Identity is one of those words. Read the words around it and ask: what would make sense here?
explain: «The police found out the thief's identity.» Here identity means who the thief really is. «Our school's identity» means the things that make the school what it is, like its culture and beliefs.
explain: Darnell shouts at the telly about VAR. VAR checks only four kinds of decision, including mistaken identity. The words around it tell you that identity here means who someone is, so the wrong person may have been named.
fact: Identity means who someone is.
fact: Identity can also mean the things that make a person or group who they are, like their name, culture and beliefs.
fact: «Identity card» and «secret identity» are phrases you will meet in everyday life and in stories.
fact: «Mistaken identity» means someone has been taken for a different person.
fact: Keep your identity safe online by never sharing your passwords.
exercise: «The police found out the thief's identity.» What does identity mean here? | The thief's favourite colour | *Who the thief really is | A lovely old hat | The way the thief runs
exercise: Which word fits? «Keep your ___ safe online by never sharing your passwords.» | glum | ancient | curt | *identity
exercise: In a story, a hero has a «secret identity». What does this mean? | A loud shout across a field | *A hidden name and life that the hero keeps private | A sore knee after football | A map of a faraway island
test: Which meaning of identity fits «our school's identity»? | Who the head teacher is | A card with a photo on it | *The things that make our school what it is, like its culture and beliefs | Being exactly the same as another school
test: Which phrase means someone has been taken for a different person? | Secret identity | Identity card | *Mistaken identity | Identity theft
exam: In «Personal identity is the question of what makes you the same person over time», what does identity mean? | A rule in football | A sudden loud noise | *What makes a person who they are | A card you show at the door
